/surname><given-names>LT</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Moser</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Dickerson</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Speck</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name> (<year>2007</year>) <article-title>Inhibition of NF-kappaB activation <italic>in vivo</italic> impairs establishment of gammaherpesvirus latency</article-title>. <source>PLoS Pathog</source> <volume>3</volume>: <fpage>e11</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17257062</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Weidmer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Volinia</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Croce</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Lieberman</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name> (<year>2008</year>) <article-title>Epstein&#x02013;Barr virus-induced miR-155 attenuates NF-kappaB signaling and stabilizes latent virus persistence</article-title>. <source>J Virol</source> <volume>82</volume>: <fpage>10436</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>10443</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18753206</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><citation citation-type="journal"><name><surname>Marques</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Efstathiou</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>KG</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Haury</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Simas</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name> (<year>2003</year>) <article-title>Selective gene expression of latent murine gammaherpesvirus 68 in B lymphocytes</article-title>. <source>J Virol</source> <volume>77</volume>: <fpage>7308</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7318</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12805429</pub-id></citation></ref><r